<p>RingZine covers professional wrestling's two biggest promotions, WWE and AEW. We publish weekly show results, premium live event and pay per view results, title changes, and roster news. Every article opens with the answer: who won, what changed, and what happens next.</p>
<h2>Confirmed or Rumor</h2>
<p>Each story carries one label at the top. <strong>Confirmed</strong> means an official WWE or AEW source backs it. <strong>Rumor</strong> means a named outlet reported it and the company has not confirmed it. The full rule is in the <a href="{{ '/editorial-policy/' | url }}">editorial policy</a>.</p>
<h2>Sources</h2>
<p>Every claim links the page it came from, and each article ends with a source list. We do not invent results, quotes, or backstage reports. Our standards are on <a href="{{ '/sources-ethics/' | url }}">Sources &amp; Ethics</a>, and errors are handled on <a href="{{ '/corrections/' | url }}">Corrections</a>.</p>
<h2>Pictures</h2>
<p>RingZine does not use WWE or AEW footage or photographs. Section images are original graphic title cards. Story images are original pictures made for RingZine, including AI generated photographs of empty rings and arenas. Each of those is labelled AI generated on the article. They are not pictures of a real show, and they do not show real people.</p>
<p>RingZine is an independent publication. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by WWE, AEW, or any wrestler named on the site. Reach us through the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">contact form</a>.</p>
